flowchart TB
  classDef human fill:#e8f0fe,stroke:#1a73e8,color:#102a43
  classDef token fill:#fef7e0,stroke:#b06000,color:#4a2c00
  classDef auto fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#188038,color:#102a43
  classDef writer fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#4a1010
  classDef external fill:#f3e8fd,stroke:#7b1fa2,color:#2b0c3d
  classDef hold fill:#f1f3f4,stroke:#5f6368,color:#202124

  operator[Repository operator / human approver]:::human
  maintainer[Trusted collaborator / reviewer]:::human
  operator --> policy[Accepted policy, capability charters, kill switches]:::human
  maintainer --> review[PR review and protected-branch checks]:::human

  policy --> gh[GitHub workflow token: least job permissions]:::token
  policy --> optoken[OPERATOR token lane: exact allowlisted action only]:::token
  policy --> provider[Configured external provider credential]:::token

  gh --> reader[Read-only/advisory workflow]:::auto
  gh --> statewriter[Bounded issue/PR/check state writer]:::writer
  gh --> fixedwriter[Fixed-path or fixed-ref repository writer]:::writer
  optoken --> peerrequest[Provider request/acknowledgement state]:::writer
  provider --> model[Gemini or OpenRouter invocation]:::external
  provider --> reviewer[CodeRabbit / opt-in peer review]:::external

  reader --> evidence[Summaries, checks, artifacts, catalogs]:::auto
  statewriter --> evidence
  fixedwriter --> postcheck[Postcondition + rollback boundary]:::writer
  peerrequest --> evidence
  model --> evidence
  reviewer --> evidence

  fixedwriter --> charter{Accepted writer tier and fixed scope?}:::hold
  charter -->|no| blocked[Separate acceptance / hold]:::hold
  charter -->|yes| postcheck
  postcheck --> review
  evidence --> review
